  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Elbit Systems of America Night Vision recorded $323M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Elbit Systems of America Night Vision won 113 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $2.9M and obligations up 8.4% year over year. Commercial and Service Industry Machinery Manufacturing is the dominant market for Elbit Systems of America Night Vision, accounting for $294M of obligations in FY2026 to date. Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing is the second-largest market with $24M in obligations. Historical yearly obligations show fluctuation: Elbit Systems of America Night Vision had $31.5M in FY21, $119M in FY22, $70.6M in FY23, $270M in FY24, and $298M in FY25. Manufacturing and Reproducing Magnetic and Optical Media accounts for $2.6M, Hardware Manufacturing accounts for $1.1M, and smaller NAICS categories include obligations of $562K, $327K, $320K, $223K, $179K, and $40.8K. The current-year totals are partial and cover fiscal year to date activity for Elbit Systems of America Night Vision.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Elbit Systems of America Night Vision’s federal business trended recently?",
        "body": "Elbit Systems of America Night Vision’s obligations rose to $323M in FY2026 to date, up 8.4% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows fluctuation: obligations were $31.5M in FY21, $119M in FY22, $70.6M in FY23, $270M in FY24, and $298M in FY25. The largest share of recent increases is concentrated in the Commercial and Service Industry Machinery Manufacturing NAICS market. Current-year totals are partial and cover fiscal year to date activity."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where do most of Elbit Systems of America Night Vision’s contract dollars go?",
        "body": "Elbit Systems of America Night Vision directs most contract dollars to Commercial and Service Industry Machinery Manufacturing, which received $294M in FY2026 to date. The next-largest NAICS is Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing with $24M, followed by Manufacturing and Reproducing Magnetic and Optical Media at $2.6M and Hardware Manufacturing at $1.1M. Smaller manufacturing categories account for the remaining obligations, including amounts of $562K, $327K, $320K, $223K, $179K, and $40.8K."
      }
    ]
